Backend routes for listing, approving, and rejecting specs stored in the workspace's specs/ directory.

File: ~/rorca/backend/src/routes/specs.ts (extend, don't replace — E-007/E-008 routes already exist)

New endpoints:

GET /api/specs?workspaceId=&status=pending|approved|all
- Scans {workspace.path}/specs/ directory for *.json files
- Parses each file to extract: specName, title (first story title), storyCount, generatedAt, approvedAt
- Status detection:
  - 'pending': exists in specs/ but NOT in specs/approved/
  - 'approved': exists in specs/approved/
- Returns array sorted by generatedAt DESC
- Response: { specs: SpecSummary[] }

```typescript
interface SpecSummary {
  id: string;           // filename without .json
  specName: string;
  storyCount: number;
  status: 'pending' | 'approved';
  generatedAt: string;
  approvedAt?: string;
  workspacePath: string;
}
```

POST /api/specs/:specId/approve
- Body: { workspaceId: string }
- Moves spec from {workspace.path}/specs/{specId}.json → {workspace.path}/specs/approved/{specId}.json
- Creates approved/ directory if it doesn't exist
- Emits WAL event: event_type='spec_approved', actor='user'
- Returns { ok: true, approvedPath: string }

POST /api/specs/:specId/reject
- Body: { workspaceId: string, reason?: string }
- Deletes spec file from specs/ (soft option: move to specs/rejected/ instead)
- Emits WAL event: event_type='spec_rejected', payload: JSON.stringify({ reason })
- Returns { ok: true }

GET /api/specs/:specId
- Returns full spec JSON content (the file contents, not a DB record)
- Searches both specs/ and specs/approved/ directories

